US-064 is implemented. The Linux and Windows gates the story lists pass, and the story's acceptance criteria are met on the toolchains available here.

**Approach.** Each scene edit is one command that stores the scene document before and after it. Undo and redo reload those documents with `Scene::load`, so GUIDs and references come back exactly. Dirty state is still the comparison with the saved text, so undoing back to the save point makes the scene clean again. A new command clears the redo steps. Opening or creating a scene clears the history.

**Choices I made:**
- **Drag merging:** a gizmo drag, and a value edited in the inspector, merge their edits into one command. The merge closes when the gesture ends, so a later drag on the same entity starts a new step.
- **Shortcuts and menu:** Ctrl+Z undoes, Ctrl+Shift+Z or Ctrl+Y redoes, and the shortcuts wait while a text field has the keyboard. An Edit menu shows the command labels, such as "Undo reparent".
- **Limits:** every command keeps two full copies of the scene document, and the history has no cap. That is fine for editor-sized scenes, but it grows with scene size and session length. This is recorded in `docs/editor.md`.

**Files changed:** `scene_editor.hpp/.cpp`, `viewport.cpp`, `editor_ui.hpp/.cpp`, `tests/src/editor_scene_tests.cpp` (8 new cases), `docs/editor.md`, and `.ralph-tui/progress.md`.

**Gates run:**
- Linux: `ValidateVendor` passes, `linux-debug` builds with warnings as errors, `linux-unit` passes (30/30), `engine_tests --suite editor` passes (64 cases, 707 assertions), and `--suite unit` passes.
- Windows, via `us064_gate.bat`: `ValidateVendor`, `win-dev` configure, `win-debug` build (no warnings), `win-unit` (29/29), `editor --backend dx12` (65 cases, 725 assertions), and `gpu --backend dx12` (72 cases, 43923 assertions) all pass.

**Not run:** the running window (no GUI check, so no screenshots or action log), the native Linux Vulkan editor suite, `linux-gcc` (GCC 11+ not installed), and `linux-asan`. The ASan preset is not required by the story's own scope, but the history does allocate memory, so it's a gap if you want that check. `engine_bench` does not apply to an editor-only change.

